      {
        "id": 140595,
        "name": "Reckless",
        "username": "Reckless",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-04-30T07:19:48.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"phantaskippy\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/48/1897_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> phantaskippy:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Reckless wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Excellent points for playing Expat with DW Fixer, Unity, and Setback.Only around 20 heroes left to go...unless the case people are making about her stagnating ammo cards is that she should exclusively play with post-SotM, pre-Tactics Darkwatch and Unity.That'd be silly.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nDon't understand your point here at all.The biggest takeaway I get from this is ammo stays behind if the gun leaves, they aren't attached. &nbsp;That means Guise can borrow a gun and the ammo will stay behind. &nbsp;The follow up question is what happens when the gun is returned, I would think the ammo is still seperate from the gun, but I don't know if that is how it will be seen officially.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I'm saying that some people are expressing disappointment at this mechanic and the reaction from some members seems to be \"Good thing these three characters allow you to benefit from this mechanic you don't enjoy!\"<br><br>It seems like a rather dismissive reaction to a frustration is all. Perhaps I was being more crass than necessary. My apologies.</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:17:32.282Z",
