      {
        "id": 140597,
        "name": "Reckless",
        "username": "Reckless",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-05-01T04:36:43.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"eugeneruss\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/a183cd/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> eugeneruss:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Sorry Reckless. I wasn’t trying to yank a chain, I was just amused by the case where for once your allies aren’t mad when you break their stuff. <img src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=12\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\"> It’s like how Absolute Zero doesn’t mind stranded ongoings, which otherwise are just a mechanical annoyance.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I can respect that perspective. Using Fueled Freeze on idle ongoings is a very satisfying experience!</p>",
