      {
        "id": 140599,
        "name": "Reckless",
        "username": "Reckless",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-05-04T20:35:53.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Medic-Tank\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/medic-tank/48/2107_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Medic-Tank:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I don't see where the drama comes from in this case. No equipment destruction EVER targets spefically guns so if you destroy your gun before the ammo it contains well your just being as stupid as destroying the cards under the self destruct sequence before the self destruct sequence… If it wasn't a coop game and the villain could target cards then it would matter.&nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>That's a little more antagonistic than I would have preferred, but that's a fair point.&nbsp; My frustration came purely from people expressing disdain at a mechanic and getting responses that there were three or four minor cases in which having a dead equipment card in play would benefit other players.&nbsp; The mechanic itself isn't terribly offensive.</p>",
